description:
Search one question at once in sources a normal web search misses: science (arXiv, Crossref), world news in 100+ languages of the last 3 months (GDELT), Internet Archive, GitHub, Wikipedia, and what people say (Bluesky, Mastodon, Lemmy, Hacker News, forums). Results grouped by source, dated, with links.
Use when: you need rich, hard-to-find, sourced information on a subject.
Example: {"query":"agentic commerce paid placement","sources":["science","news"],"lang":"en"}
